-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>van der</surname><given-names>KD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stem and progenitor cells: the premature desertion of rigorous definitions</article-title><source>Trends Neurosci</source><year>2003</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>125</fpage><lpage>131</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12591214</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Potten</surname><given-names>CS</given-names></name><name><surname>Loeffler</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Stem cells: attributes, cycles, spirals, pitfalls and uncertainties. Lessons for and from the crypt</article-title><source>Development</source><year>1990</year><volume>110</volume><fpage>1001</fpage><lpage>1020</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2100251</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Orkin</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Zon</surname><given-names>LI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hematopoiesis: an evolving paradigm for stem cell biology</article-title><source>Cell</source><year>2008</year><volume>132</volume><fpage>631</fpage><lpage>644</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18295580</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zon</surname><given-names>LI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intrinsic and extrinsic control of haematopoietic stem-cell self-renewal</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>2008</year><volume>453</volume><fpage>306</fpage><lpage>313</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18480811</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McNiece</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-t